---
title: Brisket biscuit
tags: [american, beef, smoker, weekend]
cuisine: american
source: The Briscuit by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/the-briscuit
---

> A restaurant batch: a whole 17 lb brisket and a dozen-odd biscuits. Rub the
> brisket the day before you smoke it.

== Coffee rub ==

Mix the @coffee{100%g}(medium-fine ground), @black pepper{80%g}(ground),
@kosher salt{80%g}, @granulated garlic{50%g}, @brown sugar{25%g},
@dark chile powder{12%g} and @ground cinnamon{5%g}.

== Smoked brisket ==

Coat the @brisket{17%lb}(prime, trimmed) all over with the rub, cover, and
refrigerate overnight.

Heat the #smoker{} to 250°F with charcoal and wood. Smoke the brisket to an
internal 195°F, brushing it now and then with @coffee vinegar{} and its own
juices.

Wrap in butcher paper and then foil. Heat the oven to 250°F and cook it
~{120%minutes} more. Let it cool and refrigerate.

== Jalapeño jam ==

Put the @jalapeños{1%lb}(seeded, chopped), @granulated sugar{1%cup} and
@cinnamon sticks{1/2} in a #saucepan{} and add water to cover.

Cook until the liquid is gone. Take out the cinnamon, blend the rest smooth in
a #blender{}, and refrigerate.

== Pickled onions ==

Put the @onions{2}(julienned) in a nonreactive container.

Bring the @rice vinegar{1.5%cups}, @kosher salt{1/4%cup},
@granulated sugar{1/4%cup}, @garlic{3%cloves} and a @bay leaf{} to a boil and
pour it over the onions. Cool, cover and refrigerate.

== Biscuits ==

Heat the oven to 350°F. Mix the @all-purpose flour{344%g},
@baking powder{26%g}, @granulated sugar{20%g} and @kosher salt{8%g}.

Pulse the @unsalted butter{113%g}(cubed) with 1 cup of the flour mix in a
#food processor{} until it looks like gravel.

Add the rest of the flour mix and half the @buttermilk{1.5%cups}(whole) and
work it by hand into a shaggy dough. Turn it onto a floured counter, add the
rest of the buttermilk, and fold until smooth.

Pat into a square, cut into four, stack the pieces, and press back into one
square. Cut rounds with a 3-inch #ring cutter{} and set them on a
parchment-lined #sheet tray{}.

Brush with buttermilk and bake ~{12%minutes}, turn the tray, and bake
~{13%minutes} more. Let them cool.

== Sandwich ==

Heat the oven to 350°F and warm the brisket on a sheet tray. Cut one 2-inch
slice.

Split a biscuit. Spread jalapeño jam on the bottom half, then add the brisket,
the @cheddar cheese{1%slice} and some pickled onions. Close and serve.
